SUMMARY:Josh Johnson's Comedy Band Camp LIVE at Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis (Early Show)
DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nJosh Johnson is a rising star in stand-up comedy\, best known as a writer and correspondent on The Daily Show\, where his sharp political wit and incisive cultural commentary earned him an Emmy nomination. \nHis comedy blends intelligent observation with absurdist humor\, tackling race\, politics\, and everyday life with a style that is both thought-provoking and laugh-out-loud funny. Johnson has quickly become one of the most talked-about voices in modern comedy. \nThe Comedy Band Camp concept is a unique\, immersive comedy experience — part stand-up show\, part live performance spectacle — that has been selling out theaters across the country on its 2026 tour. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, August 15\, 2026 \nTime: 5:00 PM (Early Show) \nVenue: Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis\, 910 Hennepin Avenue\, Minneapolis\, MN 55403 \nTicket Prices: $59.75 – $175 \nAge Restrictions: All ages welcome; some content may be intended for mature audiences. \nAbout the Venue\nThe Orpheum Theatre is one of Minneapolis’s most iconic and beloved performance venues\, located in the heart of the city’s vibrant Theater District on Hennepin Avenue. \nBuilt in 1921\, the Orpheum seats approximately 2\,600 guests and features stunning historic architecture\, ornate interior design\, and exceptional acoustics that make every show feel special. The venue is operated by Hennepin Theatre Trust and is renowned for hosting Broadway productions\, major concerts\, and top-tier comedy acts. \nThe Orpheum offers a mix of reserved seating options across the orchestra\, mezzanine\, and balcony levels. Amenities include multiple bars\, concession stands\, and accessible seating. Parking is available in nearby downtown Minneapolis ramps\, and the venue is easily accessible via Metro Transit light rail (Nicollet Mall Station is a short walk away). \nWhat to Expect\nJosh Johnson’s Comedy Band Camp is not your average stand-up show. Expect a high-energy\, theatrical comedy experience that combines Johnson’s razor-sharp stand-up with live musical elements and a uniquely immersive format that has wowed audiences nationwide. \nThis is the early show on Saturday\, August 15 — doors typically open 30–45 minutes before showtime. The performance runs approximately 90 minutes. Arrive early to grab a drink at the bar and soak in the gorgeous Orpheum atmosphere before the show begins. \nWhether you’re a longtime fan of Josh Johnson from The Daily Show or discovering him for the first time\, this is a must-see comedy event in Minneapolis this summer. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from $59.75 to $175 depending on seat location. Official tickets are available through Ticketmaster. Resale tickets are available through VividSeats. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at-orpheum-theatre-minneapolis-early-show/
LOCATION:Orpheum Theatre Minneapolis\, 910 Hennepin Avenue\, Minneapolis\, MN\, 55403
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://media.ticketmaster.com/en-us/dam/a/a1f/6aec4b02-7063-4485-bcc9-242f0eef6a1f_TABLET_LANDSCAPE_LARGE_16_9.jpg
GEO:34.0425006;-118.2539055
