SUMMARY:Jay Jurden LIVE at San Jose Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nJay Jurden is one of the most exciting stand-up comedians working today. His Hulu special Yes Ma’am solidifies him as one of the sharpest and most original comedic voices of his generation\, blending deeply personal storytelling with universally funny observations. \nBased in New York and originally from Mississippi\, Jay has built a reputation for precise writing\, magnetic stage presence\, and a point of view that is both intimate and hilarious. He is a four-time guest on The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon and has appeared on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert\, The Late Late Show with James Corden\, Comedy Central Featuring\, and HBO High Maintenance. \nJay served as a Staff Writer on Apple TV+ Emmy-nominated The Problem with Jon Stewart\, and his writing has appeared in The New Yorker\, Vulture\, Teen Vogue\, and McSweeney’s. In 2022\, Variety named him one of their 10 Comics to Watch\, and his debut album Jay Jurden Y’all debuted at number 1 on iTunes. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, August 15\, 2026\nShow Time: 7:00 PM PDT (Doors open at 5:30 PM)\nAdditional Shows: Sat Aug 15 at 9:30 PM and Sun Aug 16 at 6:00 PM\nVenue: San Jose Improv\, 62 S Second St\, San Jose\, CA 95113\nAge Restriction: 21+ Event – Valid ID required at the door\nContent: Stand-up comedy – sharp\, personal\, and brilliantly crafted\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe San Jose Improv is the Bay Area’s premier stand-up comedy destination\, located in the heart of downtown San Jose at 62 S Second St. Part of the nationally celebrated Improv comedy club chain\, this intimate venue has hosted some of the biggest names in comedy and remains Silicon Valley’s go-to spot for world-class stand-up. \nThe club’s cozy layout means every seat feels close to the stage\, creating an electric atmosphere that larger theaters simply cannot replicate. The venue features a full bar and dining menu\, with a mandatory two-item minimum per guest in the showroom. Seating is general admission and first-come\, first-served except for groups and premium booths\, so arriving early is strongly recommended. \nDowntown San Jose offers plenty of parking garages and easy public transit access nearby. Whether you are a longtime comedy fan or a first-timer\, the San Jose Improv delivers an unforgettable night out. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a masterclass in stand-up comedy. Jay Jurden’s live show is a high-precision\, high-energy performance that rewards attentive audiences. His material is deeply personal\, drawing from his Southern upbringing\, his identity\, and his observations on modern life\, but delivered with a wit and timing that makes it universally relatable. \nThis is a solo headlining show with no filler. Jay commands the stage with the confidence of a seasoned pro and the freshness of someone who still has plenty to say. Fans of his Hulu special will love seeing this material live\, and there is always new material that has not made it to screen yet. \nThis is a 21+ event. Bring your ID\, enjoy the two-item minimum\, and leave your phone in your pocket. No photography or recording during the show. Just pure\, undiluted comedy. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $25 – $75 (plus fees) \n\nGA Ticket: $25 (plus fees)\nPremium Banquette (seats 4): $75 (plus fees) – includes $200 food and beverage credit\, premium first-tier seating\n\nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/jay-jurden-live-at-san-jose-improv/
LOCATION:San Jose Improv\, 62 S Second St\, San Jose\, California\, 95113\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://comedycalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/64_Edp-JIrqQ0.png
