SUMMARY:The Teacher's Lounge: A Comedy Show With Rigor LIVE at The Wilbur
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performers\nThe Teacher’s Lounge: A Comedy Show With Rigor is a unique stand-up comedy show featuring three seasoned educators-turned-comedians: Gaspare Randazzo (Netflix\, The Social Studies Podcast)\, and fellow teacher-comedians who bring their classroom experiences to the stage in the most hilarious way possible. \nThese are real teachers who have traded their lesson plans for punchlines — and the result is comedy gold. Drawing from years of experience in the classroom\, they tackle the absurdities of modern education\, student behavior\, parent-teacher conferences\, and the unspoken truths of school life that only educators truly understand. Whether you’re a teacher\, a parent\, or just someone who survived school\, this show will have you laughing until it hurts. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, August 15\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM\nVenue: The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St\, Boston\, MA 02116\nDoors Open: Approximately 6:00 PM\nTicket Prices: From $39 (avg. ~$73)\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Wilbur is Boston’s premier comedy destination\, located at 246 Tremont Street in the heart of the Theatre District. This beautifully restored 1\,200-seat historic theater has been hosting world-class comedy and entertainment since 1914\, and it remains one of the most beloved venues in New England. \nThe Wilbur offers a warm\, intimate atmosphere with excellent sightlines from every seat in the house — orchestra\, mezzanine\, and balcony. A full bar is available\, and the venue’s classic architecture adds a special ambiance to every performance. The theater is conveniently located near the MBTA Boylston and Back Bay stations\, with multiple parking garages nearby on Tremont and Stuart Streets. \nWhat to Expect\nThe Teacher’s Lounge is a multi-comedian lineup show featuring some of the funniest educators in comedy today. Expect a night of relatable\, sharp\, and brilliantly observed humor about the world of teaching — from the chaos of the classroom to the politics of the faculty lounge. This is comedy that celebrates teachers while roasting the entire education system with love and laughter. \nThe show runs approximately 90 minutes and is perfect for teachers\, school staff\, parents\, and anyone who appreciates smart\, well-crafted comedy. Grab your tickets early — this unique concept show is generating serious buzz and seats are limited at The Wilbur. \nTicket Information\nTicket Prices: From $39 (average ~$73) \nSecure your seats through official Ticketmaster channels or find resale tickets through VividSeats: \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/the-teachers-lounge-a-comedy-show-with-rigor-live-at-the-wilbur/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont St.\, Boston\, MA\, 2116
